  "plain": "Dan Sheehan, an American lawyer, tells of Pat Price, a man who took part in remote viewing, the claimed practice of seeing distant places with the mind alone. Sheehan says that in the 1970s Price used this to view a file kept inside a top security facility of the CIA, the US foreign intelligence agency, and he links the story to Russell Targ and Ingo Swann, two other figures in that work, and to reports Swann wrote. If true, it would mean the mind could reach past the tightest government security."
